<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:24:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Two German officials shot dead during routine gun inspection in Bavaria; suspect arrested after overnight standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ba891221a2f3b16e4b1d8792773d524976aa288c4ec07524ad71256326a8655</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overn/live-79607225--1b63007f86d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overnight-standoff/live-79607225?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A routine inspection of legally owned firearms turned deadly in Bavaria. Police spent hours negotiating with an armed suspect before storming his home. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: UK's Burnham visits Berlin for talks with Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb5a584f875e3be832adefa313334c9e1c1d3deb14bd39ff2d7323da54b20bab</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637--034eb10b538b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham is visiting Berlin to launch a new bilateral treaty and hold talks with Chancellor Friedrich Merz. President Steinmeier is on a state visit to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa5173df581f4d9780e214fecc9b2c12814f13a792ac1c56c6e61ad168ffb4c5</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz rails against extremism, AfD sympathizers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18cdf673e6b8fbc7bf8fbcbffbed3a1a92f2c018778ebd3c5939ac86b6ff3829</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924--74b91e3a40aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political extremism threatens Germany's existing social order, Chancellor Merz has said. The Transport Ministry has proposed a five-year plan to improve Germany's ailing railroad infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany women's football team: Can Ena Mahmutovic make a case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af13874c120c14bf51f094fcf388cdc277a86dffa8124211fe47a4c27784240</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:24:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-women-s-football-team-can-ena-mahmutovic-make-a-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeepe/a-79609341--5da82027e599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-women-s-football-team-can-ena-mahmutovic-make-a-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The women's friendlies against Australia and Japan present an opportunity for Ena Mahmutovic to make her case for succeeding Ann-Katrin Berger as Germany's first-choice goalkeeper.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-German Chancellor Schröder attends Putin's birthday bash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa49672af03e293bbab964ef405f3b4dba0c4803d355f8290ba2cd3572fac47</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schr_der-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017--884ded06e661.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schröder-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Chancellor Gerhard Schröder still maintains a friendship with Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Tensions are high between Germany and Russia as the invasion of Ukraine continues.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Bundeswehr: A new naval port in Emden aims to enhance Germany's defense capabilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2620096bc3b41a747599fde206232f6b005e1ddfb3b233b8e80ac7f417331d64</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414--c280e8efd5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing the escalating security threat, Germany's Navy has decided to establish a second port on the North Sea coast. Emden was chosen as the location.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German politicians warn of antisemitism on October 7 anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e24befd214d4dafe5a41f42ae04839a4eb5e855ce0c96fb7d80d97e2cef901e3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326--969f707c1abe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leading German politicians including Chancellor Merz and President Steinmeier called for people to reject antisemitism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
